Actually, let me reconsider whether to use a global memo or a per-call memo. A global memo (package-level map) would be more efficient across benchmark iterations, but introduces a data race if Cost is called concurrently. The tests here are sequential. Exercism-style solutions typically don't use a global mutable memo. Per-call memo is cleaner and safer. Let's go with per-call.

